# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Streaming IDS — .gitignore
#
# Only patterns that can actually occur in THIS project. Docker data lives in
# named volumes (kafka-data, clickhouse-data, superset-data), not bind mounts,
# so no container state ever lands in the working tree and none is listed here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Credentials and secrets -----------------------------------------------
# The project previously carried Azure VM SSH keys in certs/. The VMs are gone
# and the keys deleted; these patterns exist so a stray key can never be
# committed by accident. Anything matching here is unrecoverable once pushed.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
certs/

# config.py reads every setting from an environment variable. The moment you
# override CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD for a non-local deployment, it belongs in a
# .env file — which must never be committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Spark Structured Streaming --------------------------------------------
# CHECKPOINT_LOCATION (config.py, default ./_checkpoints/streaming_job).
# This holds committed Kafka offsets and streaming state. Committing it is
# actively harmful: a clone would resume from another machine's offsets, and
# a stale checkpoint whose schema no longer matches makes the job refuse to
# start. Delete the directory to replay a topic from scratch.
_checkpoints/
checkpoint/
checkpoints/

# Spark's local Derby metastore and warehouse, created in the working
# directory by any local[] session — rules_engine.py's self-test and
# validate_rules.py both produce these.
spark-warehouse/
metastore_db/
derby.log

# Spark write staging and per-file checksums
.spark-staging*/
*.crc
_SUCCESS

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Packaging / tooling caches
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Run output ------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs from streaming_job.py and container output captured to file.
*.log
logs/

# Ad-hoc exports. evaluate_accuracy.py results belong in the report, not in
# git — regenerate them from ClickHouse instead of committing a snapshot.
/output/
/results/
*.parquet

# --- Editors ---------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- OS --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Windows (development machine)
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# macOS (in case the repo is opened or marked up elsewhere)
.DS_Store
._*
